WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:09.430
On the 22nd of July this summer, my father passed away.

2
00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:13.720
It was in the summer, a few days before, I got a phone call.

3
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.030
I was in Tryavna. I was about to run the Tryavna ultramarathon.

4
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:20.320
So, I ran. I came back home.

5
00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:24.040
I still saw him that night before he was given his last morphine

6
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:26.880
shot. And then there were 52 hours.

7
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.950
That was Wednesday, and then he passed away.

8
00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.750
Why am I telling you this?

9
00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:35.360
First, if you have not talked to your parents in a long time,

10
00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:37.550
you might want to do it during the coffee break.

11
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:43.760
Second reason is what I saw was the most perfect irreversible human

12
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:48.960
shutdown of a body. When somebody dies, all the vital organs start

13
00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:50.440
failing one after the other.

14
00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:53.550
And the last one is obviously the heart and the last breath.

15
00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.830
Now, this is not what you want for cybersecurity.

16
00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.520
Cybersecurity is protecting data, networks, and systems.

17
00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.920
And so, when you finish your work, you close your laptop,

18
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.910
the next day you want it to just restart.

19
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.840
When you have an update or patches, you want it to restart again.

20
00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.270
And if you have a problem and you ask your IT department,

21
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.310
you want it to reboot, to be alive and back again.

22
00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:19.120
And that's possible. You need foundations.

23
00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.240
You need to be solid. And there you are.

24
00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.070
